 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Relates to coverage for eating disorders; requires comparable coverage for adults and children with eating disorders; defines eating disorder.",
 "title": "Relates to coverage for eating disorders",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A1619",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A1619-2019",
     "printNo": "A1619",
     "session": 2019,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 241\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 1619, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  insurance law, in relation to coverage for\n      eating disorders\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require insurance companies to provide  full  coverage\nfor  the  treatment  of eating disorders. As defined in the bill, eating\ndisorders would mean: pica,  rumination  disorder,  avoidant/restrictive\nfood  intake  disorder,  anorexia nervosa, bulimia nervosa, binge eating\ndisorder, other specified feeding or  eating  disorder,  and  any  other\neating  disorder  contained in the most recent version of the Diagnostic\nand Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM) published by the Ameri-\ncan Psychiatric Association.\n \n  While I am supportive of  the  intent,  these  diagnoses  are  already\ncovered  in  the  Insurance  Law, as amended by the 2020 enacted budget.\nUnder existing law, insurers are required to cover  \"biologically  based\nmental     illnesses,\"     including    pica,    rumination    disorder,\navoidant/restrictive food intake  disorder,  anorexia  nervosa,  bulimia\nnervosa, binge eating disorder, other specified feeding or eating disor-\nder,  and  any  other  eating  disorder.  The enacted budget amended the\nInsurance Law to require insurance coverage for the diagnosis and treat-\nment of substance use disorder and mental  health  conditions  that  are\nlisted in the most recent version of the DSM.\n \n  This  bill,  was  not  updated to reflect the changes made by the 2020\nenacted budget, and in fact amends sections of law that will be repealed\nJanuary 1, 2020 which already provides this coverage.  The  changes  put\nforth  in  this  bill  are unnecessary and could cause confusion if this\nbill were to be signed. Accordingly, I cannot support this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 241,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2019
   }
